# Skill Index

Match intent below, then load only the selected `<skill>/SKILL.md` and references it requests. Prefer one narrow domain owner; add review/safety lenses only when needed. Simple formatting, renames and config-value edits need no skill.

This is an installation discovery map. Concrete skill names belong here and in WIRING; reusable skill bundles describe capability handoffs without depending on sibling identities or paths.

For non-trivial work, load `team-operating-model` before substantive work: activation requires a real primary-plus-worker team; unavailable permitted delegation blocks affected work, never solo/simulated fallback. Exclude trivial work before activation. `subagent-dispatch` governs every worker launch; skill selection grants no launch or implementation authority.

