## Routing Rules

- **Planning/specifications:** use [lightweight planning](working-principles/references/planning.md) as needed. Product intent → `brainstorming`; technical constraints → `architecture-design`; behavior/BDD/acceptance → `code-craft`; journeys/states → `ui-ux`; presentation → `doc-craft`. No mandatory artifact ladder; specification authority is not implementation authority.
- **Reviews:** narrow reviews use the matching lens; broad/mixed/deep reviews use `reviewer` (or an available built-in review command). **Governance:** `skill-author` audit/modify; `project-foundation` for pack/foundation gaps. **Project setup:** foundation before `devsecops` hardening.
- **Investing:** `investment-assessment` owns allocation/diligence; team finance deliberation or reviewer `investment-memo` supplies warranted challenge, not a separate default credit skill.
- **Documents:** [format selection](doc-craft/references/document-formats.md) preserves native/existing formats; concise entries in Markdown, comprehensive human-facing detail in Typst/PDF. Management reports use `../docs/ai-augmented-project-setup-and-evolution.md` §9 for topics, not a fixed workflow/template.
- **Maintenance:** project indexes include core pack + actually used skills, not the entire global catalog. Keep detailed methods in skill bodies/references; see [WIRING](WIRING) for composition and handoffs.
